{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useThrottler<TFn, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): ReactThrottler<TFn, TSelected>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/react-pacer/src/throttler/useThrottler.ts#L168","children":[{"type":"text","value":"throttler/useThrottler.ts:168"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A low-level React hook that creates a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Throttler"},{"type":"text","value":" instance that limits how often the provided function can execute."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This hook is designed to be flexible and state-management agnostic - it simply returns a throttler instance that\nyou can integrate with any state management solution (useState, Redux, Zustand, Jotai, etc). For a simpler and higher-level hook that\nintegrates directly with React's useState, see useThrottledState."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Throttling ensures a function executes at most once within a specified time window,\nregardless of how many times it is called. This is useful for rate-limiting\nexpensive operations or UI updates."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-management-and-selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management and Selector"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook uses TanStack Store for reactive state management. You can subscribe to state changes\nin two ways:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"throttler.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" HOC (Recommended for component tree subscriptions)"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" HOC to subscribe to state changes deep in your component tree without\nneeding to pass a selector to the hook. This is ideal when you want to subscribe to state\nin child components."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selector"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter (For hook-level subscriptions)"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selector"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger a re-render\nat the hook level, optimizing performance by preventing unnecessary re-renders when irrelevant\nstate changes occur."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function or using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" HOC. This prevents unnecessary\nre-renders and gives you full control over when your component updates."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available state properties:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"executionCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of function executions that have been completed"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastArgs"},{"type":"text","value":": The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastExecutionTime"},{"type":"text","value":": Timestamp of the last function execution in milliseconds"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nextExecutionTime"},{"type":"text","value":": Timestamp when the next execution can occur in milliseconds"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPending"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the throttler is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":": Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending')"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"unmount-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unmount behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, the hook cancels any pending execution when the component unmounts.\nUse the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUnmount"},{"type":"text","value":" option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const throttler = useThrottler(fn, {\n  wait: 1000,\n  onUnmount: (t) => t.flush()\n});","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyFunction"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/ReactThrottlerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactThrottlerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/ReactThrottler.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactThrottler"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0);\nconst throttler = useThrottler(setValue, { wait: 1000 });\n\n// Subscribe to state changes deep in component tree using Subscribe HOC\n<throttler.Subscribe selector={(state) => ({ isPending: state.isPending })}>\n  {({ isPending }) => (\n    <div>{isPending ? 'Throttling...' : 'Ready'}</div>\n  )}\n</throttler.Subscribe>\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when execution count changes at hook level (optimized for tracking executions)\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0);\nconst throttler = useThrottler(\n  setValue,\n  { wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({ executionCount: state.executionCount })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when throttling state changes (optimized for loading indicators)\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0);\nconst throttler = useThrottler(\n  setValue,\n  { wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({\n    isPending: state.isPending,\n    status: state.status\n  })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when timing information changes (optimized for timing displays)\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0);\nconst throttler = useThrottler(\n  setValue,\n  { wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({\n    lastExecutionTime: state.lastExecutionTime,\n    nextExecutionTime: state.nextExecutionTime\n  })\n);\n\n// With any state manager\nconst throttler = useThrottler(\n  (value) => stateManager.setState(value),\n  {\n    wait: 2000,\n    leading: true,   // Execute immediately on first call\n    trailing: false  // Skip trailing edge updates\n  }\n);\n\n// Access the selected state (will be empty object {} unless selector provided)\nconst { executionCount, isPending } = throttler.state;","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"state-management-and-selector","text":"State Management and Selector","level":2},{"id":"unmount-behavior","text":"Unmount behavior","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfn","text":"TFn","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useThrottler<TFn, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): ReactThrottler<TFn, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [throttler/useThrottler.ts:168](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/react-pacer/src/throttler/useThrottler.ts#L168)\n\nA low-level React hook that creates a `Throttler` instance that limits how often the provided function can execute.\n\nThis hook is designed to be flexible and state-management agnostic - it simply returns a throttler instance that\nyou can integrate with any state management solution (useState, Redux, Zustand, Jotai, etc). For a simpler and higher-level hook that\nintegrates directly with React's useState, see useThrottledState.\n\nThrottling ensures a function executes at most once within a specified time window,\nregardless of how many times it is called. This is useful for rate-limiting\nexpensive operations or UI updates.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe hook uses TanStack Store for reactive state management. You can subscribe to state changes\nin two ways:\n\n**1. Using `throttler.Subscribe` HOC (Recommended for component tree subscriptions)**\n\nUse the `Subscribe` HOC to subscribe to state changes deep in your component tree without\nneeding to pass a selector to the hook. This is ideal when you want to subscribe to state\nin child components.\n\n**2. Using the `selector` parameter (For hook-level subscriptions)**\n\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger a re-render\nat the hook level, optimizing performance by preventing unnecessary re-renders when irrelevant\nstate changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function or using the `Subscribe` HOC. This prevents unnecessary\nre-renders and gives you full control over when your component updates.\n\nAvailable state properties:\n- `executionCount`: Number of function executions that have been completed\n- `lastArgs`: The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute\n- `lastExecutionTime`: Timestamp of the last function execution in milliseconds\n- `nextExecutionTime`: Timestamp when the next execution can occur in milliseconds\n- `isPending`: Whether the throttler is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution\n- `status`: Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending')\n\n## Unmount behavior\n\nBy default, the hook cancels any pending execution when the component unmounts.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:\n\n```tsx\nconst throttler = useThrottler(fn, {\n  wait: 1000,\n  onUnmount: (t) => t.flush()\n});\n```\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyFunction`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`ReactThrottlerOptions`](../interfaces/ReactThrottlerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`ReactThrottler`](../interfaces/ReactThrottler.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0);\nconst throttler = useThrottler(setValue, { wait: 1000 });\n\n// Subscribe to state changes deep in component tree using Subscribe HOC\n<throttler.Subscribe selector={(state) => ({ isPending: state.isPending })}>\n  {({ isPending }) => (\n    <div>{isPending ? 'Throttling...' : 'Ready'}</div>\n  )}\n</throttler.Subscribe>\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when execution count changes at hook level (optimized for tracking executions)\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0);\nconst throttler = useThrottler(\n  setValue,\n  { wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({ executionCount: state.executionCount })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when throttling state changes (optimized for loading indicators)\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0);\nconst throttler = useThrottler(\n  setValue,\n  { wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({\n    isPending: state.isPending,\n    status: state.status\n  })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when timing information changes (optimized for timing displays)\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0);\nconst throttler = useThrottler(\n  setValue,\n  { wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({\n    lastExecutionTime: state.lastExecutionTime,\n    nextExecutionTime: state.nextExecutionTime\n  })\n);\n\n// With any state manager\nconst throttler = useThrottler(\n  (value) => stateManager.setState(value),\n  {\n    wait: 2000,\n    leading: true,   // Execute immediately on first call\n    trailing: false  // Skip trailing edge updates\n  }\n);\n\n// Access the selected state (will be empty object {} unless selector provided)\nconst { executionCount, isPending } = throttler.state;\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useThrottler\ntitle: useThrottler\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useThrottler<TFn, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): ReactThrottler<TFn, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [throttler/useThrottler.ts:168](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/react-pacer/src/throttler/useThrottler.ts#L168)\n\nA low-level React hook that creates a `Throttler` instance that limits how often the provided function can execute.\n\nThis hook is designed to be flexible and state-management agnostic - it simply returns a throttler instance that\nyou can integrate with any state management solution (useState, Redux, Zustand, Jotai, etc). For a simpler and higher-level hook that\nintegrates directly with React's useState, see useThrottledState.\n\nThrottling ensures a function executes at most once within a specified time window,\nregardless of how many times it is called. This is useful for rate-limiting\nexpensive operations or UI updates.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe hook uses TanStack Store for reactive state management. You can subscribe to state changes\nin two ways:\n\n**1. Using `throttler.Subscribe` HOC (Recommended for component tree subscriptions)**\n\nUse the `Subscribe` HOC to subscribe to state changes deep in your component tree without\nneeding to pass a selector to the hook. This is ideal when you want to subscribe to state\nin child components.\n\n**2. Using the `selector` parameter (For hook-level subscriptions)**\n\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger a re-render\nat the hook level, optimizing performance by preventing unnecessary re-renders when irrelevant\nstate changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function or using the `Subscribe` HOC. This prevents unnecessary\nre-renders and gives you full control over when your component updates.\n\nAvailable state properties:\n- `executionCount`: Number of function executions that have been completed\n- `lastArgs`: The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute\n- `lastExecutionTime`: Timestamp of the last function execution in milliseconds\n- `nextExecutionTime`: Timestamp when the next execution can occur in milliseconds\n- `isPending`: Whether the throttler is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution\n- `status`: Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending')\n\n## Unmount behavior\n\nBy default, the hook cancels any pending execution when the component unmounts.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:\n\n```tsx\nconst throttler = useThrottler(fn, {\n  wait: 1000,\n  onUnmount: (t) => t.flush()\n});\n```\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyFunction`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`ReactThrottlerOptions`](../interfaces/ReactThrottlerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`ReactThrottler`](../interfaces/ReactThrottler.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0);\nconst throttler = useThrottler(setValue, { wait: 1000 });\n\n// Subscribe to state changes deep in component tree using Subscribe HOC\n<throttler.Subscribe selector={(state) => ({ isPending: state.isPending })}>\n  {({ isPending }) => (\n    <div>{isPending ? 'Throttling...' : 'Ready'}</div>\n  )}\n</throttler.Subscribe>\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when execution count changes at hook level (optimized for tracking executions)\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0);\nconst throttler = useThrottler(\n  setValue,\n  { wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({ executionCount: state.executionCount })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when throttling state changes (optimized for loading indicators)\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0);\nconst throttler = useThrottler(\n  setValue,\n  { wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({\n    isPending: state.isPending,\n    status: state.status\n  })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when timing information changes (optimized for timing displays)\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0);\nconst throttler = useThrottler(\n  setValue,\n  { wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({\n    lastExecutionTime: state.lastExecutionTime,\n    nextExecutionTime: state.nextExecutionTime\n  })\n);\n\n// With any state manager\nconst throttler = useThrottler(\n  (value) => stateManager.setState(value),\n  {\n    wait: 2000,\n    leading: true,   // Execute immediately on first call\n    trailing: false  // Skip trailing edge updates\n  }\n);\n\n// Access the selected state (will be empty object {} unless selector provided)\nconst { executionCount, isPending } = throttler.state;\n```\n"}
